# A turn of the walk loads the value and the next link, adds, and compares the next link with null. That one comparison is both the end of the loop and the proof for the loads of the next turn: the link is not tested again, and its shape is not looked at.
# CHECK-LABEL: loop #
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[link]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[value]] = Load(b@[[link]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[next]] = Load(b@[[link]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@[[value]], b@{{*}}, {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isNull]] = Equal(b@[[next]], $2(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNull]], Terminal
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# NONE-LABEL: loop #
# NONE-NOT: AOTObject_shapeWord
# NONE-NOT: JSCell_typeInfoType
# NONE-NOT: BitAnd(
# NONE-COUNT-1: Branch(
# NONE-NOT: Branch(
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
# The patchpoint is the poll of the loop.
# X64: instructions: 5, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 1
